---
interface Props {
	title: string;
	description: string;
}

const { title, description } = Astro.props;
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<meta charset="utf-8" />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
		<meta name="generator" content={Astro.generator} />
		<title>{title}</title>
		<meta name="description" content={description} />
		<meta name="color-scheme" content="dark" />
		{/*
			Mirrors --color-bg in src/styles/global.css. A meta tag cannot read a CSS custom property,
			and without it a phone browser paints its own light chrome above a dark page.
		*/}
		<meta name="theme-color" content="#0d1311" />
		{/*
			The whole privacy claim of this app is "your token only ever goes to
			classic.warcraftlogs.com". A connect-src policy is the only version of that claim a visitor
			can verify without reading our source, so ship one — the browser, not our code, enforces it.
			It names the single MoP host rather than a wildcard, because that is the only host this app
			has any business reaching. Production-only, because `astro dev` talks to an HMR websocket
			this would block.
		*/}
		{
			import.meta.env.PROD && (
				<meta
					http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy"
					content="connect-src 'self' https://classic.warcraftlogs.com; img-src 'self' data: https://wow.zamimg.com; form-action 'none'; base-uri 'none'"
				/>
			)
		}
	</head>
	<body>
		{/*
			Wowhead's tooltip widget, which is the one third-party script this page loads.
			
			It exists because the gear section shows items by icon, and an icon with no name is a
			picture of a puzzle. The log gives an item id and nothing else — no name, no stats — so the
			only way to say what a piece *is* comes from Wowhead, and their widget is how they publish
			it. It attaches to any link pointing at one of their item or spell pages.

			What this costs, stated plainly because the README makes a promise about it: hovering an
			item tells wowhead.com that someone looked at that item. It is loaded from the same image
			host the icons already come from, it is deferred so it never blocks the report, and it sees
			nothing else on the page — no token, which lives in sessionStorage and is never in the DOM,
			and no report code, which is in the URL but not passed to them.

			Injected from a bundled module rather than written inline so the policy below can name
			'self' instead of 'unsafe-inline'.
		*/}
		<script>
			// The widget reads this before it initialises. Left plain: recolouring and renaming the
			// report's own links to match Wowhead's house style would fight the design.
			Object.assign(window, { whTooltips: { colorLinks: false, iconizeLinks: false, renameLinks: false } });

			const widget = document.createElement('script');
			widget.src = 'https://wow.zamimg.com/widgets/power.js';
			widget.defer = true;
			document.head.append(widget);
		</script>
		<slot />
	</body>
</html>
